Before export, the validator recorded node names, mesh and triangle counts from
each GLB and SHA-256 hashes for 59 source .blend/export PNG/installed prop PNG
files. After export it checked GLB headers, declared binary lengths, node-set
differences, triangle counts, absence of Studio shadow-helper nodes/materials,
absence of external buffer/image URIs, and all protected hashes.

The six-case regression executed the actual export_glb method extracted from
studio.py with mocked Blender selection/export APIs. A matching Studio helper
and one with a Blender numeric material suffix were omitted. A real entrance
shadow, a similarly named larger mesh, a quad with a different material, and a
quad without the Studio UV marker were retained.

